      "content": "but that's the thing, even if i make it \"bearable\" for myself, it doesn't change the reality of it. i'm just choosing to prolong a cycle of struggle in a way that has zero lasting impact. if the math shows that everything is temporary and ultimately zero, isn't it more \"logical\" to just accept the void? why is it considered \"better\" to keep fighting a losing battle against entropy just for a bit of temporary comfort? it feels like we're just clinging to nothing.",
